item.text:
**Reused evidence**
None. The existing reusable items in the thread were not germane to Chapter 5B, so I did not reuse any prior evidence.

**New evidence**
Accepted source-claim units below are the retained, non-duplicative 5B evidence. I kept the record centered on 2022 appointment choices, macro/fiscal management, investment and tax reform, household distribution, and anti-corruption/capture signals.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Factbox-Key figures in Philippine President Marcos' administration","publisher":"Reuters (syndicated via MarketScreener)","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Factbox-Key-figures-in-Philippine-President-Marcos-administration-40857917/","claim":"Reuters described Benjamin Diokno as a two-time budget minister who would lead Marcos's economic team, Arsenio Balisacan as returning as planning chief, and Felipe Medalla as incoming central bank governor, indicating a technocratic core for the new administration.","locator":"search result excerpt under Benjamin Diokno, Arsenio Balisacan, and Felipe Medalla","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters factbox with named appointments and role descriptions; independent and specific to the 2022 transition.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers pre-inauguration 2022 appointments that shaped the target-year economic team.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos's cabinet choices.","contrary_evidence":["Competence is inferred from resumes, not proven by 2022 outcomes.","The broader cabinet still mixed technocrats with political figures."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.3","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Diokno bares six-year plan for fiscal stability and economic development","publisher":"Department of Finance","publication_date":"2022-07-08","url":"https://www.dof.gov.ph/diokno-bares-six-year-plan-for-fiscal-stability-and-economic-development/","claim":"Diokno said the Marcos administration's first Medium-Term Fiscal Framework was aimed at reducing the deficit, promoting fiscal sustainability, and enabling robust growth.","locator":"lead paragraph and MTFF quote","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official announcement of a dated fiscal plan with explicit targets.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022 and about the administration's medium-term plan.","ruler_attribution":"Direct at the administration level, though the source is still a plan rather than execution.","contrary_evidence":["Plan stage only; implementation and results are not established here.","Growth outcomes also depended on inherited post-pandemic recovery."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippines: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; and Staff Report","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-12-15","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/12/15/philippines-2022-article-iv-consultation-press-release-and-staff-report-526983","claim":"The IMF said a new administration took office in July with a blueprint for an inclusive, sustainable, and green recovery, but the economy still faced the need for the right policy mix, stronger fiscal buffers, and higher long-term growth.","locator":"Summary section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent multilateral assessment with an explicit policy diagnosis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year 2022 assessment.","ruler_attribution":"Partly attributable to Marcos's policy direction after July 2022; macro outcomes also reflected inherited fundamentals and global shocks.","contrary_evidence":["Inflation and fiscal space had deteriorated by late 2022.","The report also says the outlook was challenged by a difficult global environment."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Monetary Policy Report May 2022","publisher":"Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas","publication_date":"2022-05-19","url":"https://www.bsp.gov.ph/SitePages/PriceStability/FullReportMPR/MonetaryPolicyReport_Full_May2022.aspx","claim":"Before Marcos took office, BSP raised the policy rate to 2.25 percent and projected 2022 inflation above target at 4.6 percent, citing food, energy, and supply pressures.","locator":"Monetary Policy Summary and Economic Outlook","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official monetary policy report with explicit forecast and policy action.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Pre-inauguration baseline for the 2022 year.","ruler_attribution":"Inherited baseline only; not attributable to Marcos.","contrary_evidence":["This source predates Marcos's June 30 inauguration.","It reflects inherited inflation pressures rather than Marcos policy."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippine central bank hastens interest rate rise, ready for more action","publisher":"Reuters (syndicated via Investing.com)","publication_date":"2022-07-13","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/philippine-central-bank-makes-surprise-75-bps-hike-in-interest-rates-2847038","claim":"Reuters reported that BSP raised rates by 75 basis points off-cycle to contain broadening inflationary pressure and rescue a faltering peso.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a specific, dated policy action and motive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: monetary policy was central-bank action, but it responded to the macro environment the Marcos administration faced.","contrary_evidence":["The move was by the independent central bank, not the president directly.","It shows crisis management more than a Marcos-originated policy."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippines Economic Updates","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-06-08","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/philippines/publication/philippine-economic-updates","claim":"The World Bank said the Philippines was poised to grow 5.7 percent in 2022 and that continuity of growth- and investment-supporting policies was key to strengthening recovery.","locator":"June 2022 entry on the economic updates page","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent multilateral growth forecast and policy assessment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022.","ruler_attribution":"Partly baseline and partly policy-continuity advice; not a direct score of Marcos's implementation.","contrary_evidence":["Growth forecast was based on domestic recovery conditions that predated the administration.","The report also notes external and global uncertainty."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"NEDA to flesh out development agenda for addressing constraints to inclusive growth","publisher":"Philippine Information Agency / NEDA","publication_date":"2022-08-03","url":"https://mirror.pia.gov.ph/press-releases/2022/08/03/neda-to-flesh-out-development-agenda-for-addressing-constraints-to-inclusive-growth","claim":"NEDA said the Marcos administration's 8-point socioeconomic agenda would address short-term inflation and shock vulnerability, and longer-term job creation, infrastructure, logistics, energy, digitalization, regulation, and governance.","locator":"lead paragraphs and Balisacan quote","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official release quoting NEDA's implementation agenda and priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct at the administration level.","contrary_evidence":["It is an agenda statement, not implementation.","The source is official and promotional."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.7","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PH socioeconomic agenda presented at IMF, World Bank meeting","publisher":"Philippine News Agency","publication_date":"2022-10-14","url":"https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1186116","claim":"Marcos's economic managers said the 8-point socioeconomic agenda aimed to cut poverty to 9 percent by the end of the six-year term and raise the Philippines to upper-middle-income status by 2028.","locator":"lead paragraph and agenda bullet list","source_type":"official/newswire","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Dated report on official targets announced by the administration.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct on the administration's target-setting.","contrary_evidence":["Aspirational target, not observed outcome.","The source is a government newswire."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Marcos relays food production agenda in 1st SONA","publisher":"Department of Agriculture","publication_date":"2022-07-26","url":"https://www.da.gov.ph/marcos-relays-food-production-agenda-in-1st-sona/","claim":"Marcos said agriculture would be one of the main drivers of growth and employment and that his administration would fight food-price spikes by increasing production and supporting consumers' purchasing power.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted statement","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential directive within the target year, reported on an official agency page.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target year 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct.","contrary_evidence":["The source is self-reporting and policy intent, not implementation.","The food-price problem was partly inherited and global."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.6","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Senate approves 2023 national budget on third reading","publisher":"Department of Finance","publication_date":"2022-11-25","url":"https://www.dof.gov.ph/senate-approves-2023-national-budget-on-third-reading/","claim":"The Marcos administration's first approved appropriations law increased funding for education, agriculture for food security, health, labor and employment, tourism, public works, and energy.","locator":"second and third paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific budget allocation with executive attribution and concrete sectoral priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Passed in 2022 as the first budget under Marcos for FY2023.","ruler_attribution":"Direct at the administration level; implementation follows later.","contrary_evidence":["Budget approval does not prove spending quality or execution.","Some increases mainly continue existing programs."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deeper Participation in Global Value Chains Will Strengthen Recovery and Competitiveness of the Philippine Economy","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-06","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/06/deeper-participation-in-gvcs-will-strengthen-recovery-and-competitiveness-of-ph-econ","claim":"The World Bank said the Philippines needed to ease FDI restrictions and address skills and connectivity gaps, noting that amendments to the Foreign Investments Act, Retail Trade Liberalization Act, and Public Service Act were relevant to attracting investment.","locator":"middle paragraphs on structural constraints and reforms","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent policy analysis with a concrete reform list and clear period fit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022.","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the reforms were partly inherited or legislative, but Marcos's administration was responsible for implementation and promotion in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["The report also makes clear that structural constraints persisted.","Some reforms were inherited rather than originated by Marcos."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Marcos admin streamlines private sector participation processes to encourage investments","publisher":"Department of Finance","publication_date":"2022-10-24","url":"https://www.dof.gov.ph/marcos-admin-streamlines-private-sector-participation-processes-to-encourage-investments/","claim":"DOF said the Marcos administration had streamlined private-sector participation through amended investment laws and revised BOT rules to make PPPs more attractive and to secure domestic and foreign investment.","locator":"lead paragraphs and Diokno quote","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific administration policy and implementation step, dated in 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct at the administration level, though the law changes partly built on prior reforms.","contrary_evidence":["The source is official and promotional.","Implementation benefits were projected, not yet fully evidenced."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DOF unveils fiscal priority reforms under Marcos admin","publisher":"Department of Finance","publication_date":"2022-08-19","url":"https://www.dof.gov.ph/dof-unveils-fiscal-priority-reforms-under-marcos-admin/","claim":"DOF said the Marcos administration's MTFF included real-property valuation reform to broaden the tax base and promote a just, equitable, and efficient valuation system.","locator":"lead paragraph and quoted explanation","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Explicit reform text tied to the administration.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct at the administration level.","contrary_evidence":["Proposed reform only; not proof of enactment or anti-corruption impact.","The source is a ministry announcement."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PHILIPPINES: Reducing Inequality Key to Becoming a Middle-Class Society Free of Poverty","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-11-24","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/11/24/ph-reducing-inequality-key-to-becoming-a-middle-class-society-free-of-poverty","claim":"The World Bank said poverty reduction gains were substantial but inequality remained high, with the top 1 percent capturing 17 percent of national income and the bottom 50 percent receiving only 14 percent.","locator":"report summary and inequality paragraph","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent distributional evidence with concrete shares.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 distributional context for Marcos's first months.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly inherited baseline and structural conditions; useful as context for the trajectory the administration inherited.","contrary_evidence":["The report also credits sustained growth, education, jobs, and social assistance for earlier poverty reduction.","The data are not a direct measure of Marcos-specific 2022 outcomes."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PSA releases the 2022 Statistical Indicators on Philippine Development","publisher":"Philippine Statistics Authority","publication_date":"2023-07-17","url":"https://psa.gov.ph/content/psa-releases-2022-statistical-indicators-philippine-development","claim":"PSA said StatDev 2022 showed the Philippines made progress on some development goals, with only four of 15 sectoral chapters at average performance and six of nine core indicators meeting targets.","locator":"lead summary paragraphs","source_type":"official/statistical","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statistical synthesis with year-specific targets and outcomes.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective 2022 summary published in 2023.","ruler_attribution":"Mixed: combines inherited conditions and Marcos-year implementation; not a direct causal estimate.","contrary_evidence":["The same summary says many indicators were still off track.","It is an aggregate planning metric, not a ruler-specific causal estimate."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Marcos' 1st edict abolishes PACC, Office of CabSec","publisher":"Philippine News Agency","publication_date":"2022-07-07","url":"https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1178410","claim":"Marcos's first executive order abolished the Presidential Anti-Corruption Commission and transferred its functions to the Office of the Deputy Executive Secretary for Legal Affairs in the name of bureaucracy simplification.","locator":"lead paragraphs and EO 1 summary","source_type":"official/newswire","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of a dated executive order and its terms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct.","contrary_evidence":["The administration said the move was to streamline duplicated functions, so the anti-corruption meaning is contested.","The PACC was itself a relatively new and executive-controlled body."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gov't told not to abolish PCGG during Marcos rule","publisher":"BusinessWorld","publication_date":"2022-08-28","url":"https://www.bworldonline.com/the-nation/2022/08/28/471054/govt-told-not-to-abolish-pcgg-during-marcos-rule/","claim":"Analysts said the PCGG should not be abolished during Marcos's rule because of conflict-of-interest concerns and the unresolved Marcos ill-gotten-wealth cases.","locator":"article lead and quoted analyst comments","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Reporting on a live policy debate with direct conflict-of-interest rationale, but it is still an analysis piece rather than a formal finding.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: the concern arises specifically from Marcos's family history and administration.","contrary_evidence":["It is an analyst view, not a formal legal finding.","Officials argued the agency had outlived usefulness."],"lenses":["5B.5"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across Reuters-syndicated reporting, IMF, World Bank, BSP, DOF, DA, NEDA/PIA, PNA, PSA, and BusinessWorld. I retained 16 distinct URLs above and rejected the rest for one of four reasons.

- Duplicate or near-duplicate removals: multiple articles repeated the same 2022 economic team appointments, the same 8-point socioeconomic agenda, the same food-security directive, or the same inflation response. I kept one or two sources per distinct policy move rather than padding the record.
- Weak or promotional removals: several official pages restated the administration's own intentions without adding new facts, so I kept only the strongest official item per policy family and paired it with independent multilateral or Reuters corroboration where possible.
- Blocked or awkwardly accessible removals: some PCO/SONA pages and IMF eLibrary pages were partially blocked or difficult to open cleanly, so I relied on accessible mirrors, search-result excerpts, or alternate official pages carrying the same claim.
- Out-of-period or later follow-ups removed: 2023-2024 budget, PPP, tax, and food-price follow-ups were excluded unless they explicitly described a 2022 act or 2022 policy direction. I did not use later material to expand the 2022 period silently.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct anti-corruption and capture evidence is still thin. The record shows one early simplification move that cut an anti-corruption body and one criticism about the Marcos wealth-recovery commission, but I did not find strong 2022 evidence of effective anti-corruption enforcement or capture reversal.
- Distributional evidence is better on poverty and inequality than on regions, classes, or gender-specific outcomes. More 2022 FIES/PSA subnational breakdowns or labor-income microdata would improve lens 5B.8.
- The macro record is strong on plans and independent assessments, but only partly on Marcos-specific implementation. More budget-execution, procurement, and program-delivery sources would help separate inherited recovery from ruler-attributed change.
- The evidence on competence of the economic team is strong on resumes and appointments, but weaker on whether Marcos actually empowered those professionals versus merely naming them. More cabinet minutes, delegation records, and implementation follow-through would help.
